        "id": 5334,
        "name": "Christopher",
        "username": "Christopher",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-11-17T14:31:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ok, people.  I don’t know if you’re familiar with the awesome product <a href=\"http://www.gamingpaper.com/\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Gaming Paper</a>, but it makes my life significantly better, and I was thrilled to get to meet and hang out with Erik Bauer, the creator of Gaming Paper, at Gen Con this year!  Very cool guy - all the Gaming Paper folks were great, really.  However!  They are now working on making some TOTALLY AWESOME gift wrap, which is good, as the vast majority of gift wrap I buy falls into the, “eh, this is good enough, and not terribly offensive to my eyes.”  <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/gamingpaper/cthulhu-wrap\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">THIS STUFF</a> is awesome.  Seriously awesome.  I mean, come on - who DOESN’T want their gifts wrapped in Elder Signs and Elder Gods?  Right?  RIGHT?!</p>\n<p>So, go <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/gamingpaper/cthulhu-wrap\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">check out their Kickstarter</a> - it only had a couple of days left, and it would be really awesome to see this cool and fun project funded!  Really, I’m posting this for entirely selfish reasons.  I want to buy Cthulhu wrapping paper!  If it doesn’t get funded, my pledge doesn’t go through, and I don’t get my precious rolls of sweet, terrifying gift wrap!  Any takers?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:57.365Z",
