        "raw": "Ok, people.  I don't know if you're familiar with the awesome product [url=http://www.gamingpaper.com/]Gaming Paper[/url], but it makes my life significantly better, and I was thrilled to get to meet and hang out with Erik Bauer, the creator of Gaming Paper, at Gen Con this year!  Very cool guy - all the Gaming Paper folks were great, really.  However!  They are now working on making some TOTALLY AWESOME gift wrap, which is good, as the vast majority of gift wrap I buy falls into the, \"eh, this is good enough, and not terribly offensive to my eyes.\"  [url=http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/gamingpaper/cthulhu-wrap]THIS STUFF[/url] is awesome.  Seriously awesome.  I mean, come on - who DOESN'T want their gifts wrapped in Elder Signs and Elder Gods?  Right?  RIGHT?!  \n\nSo, go [url=http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/gamingpaper/cthulhu-wrap]check out their Kickstarter[/url] - it only had a couple of days left, and it would be really awesome to see this cool and fun project funded!  Really, I'm posting this for entirely selfish reasons.  I want to buy Cthulhu wrapping paper!  If it doesn't get funded, my pledge doesn't go through, and I don't get my precious rolls of sweet, terrifying gift wrap!  Any takers?",
